-- statement:
--   The theorem states that for every natural number n>0 with n different from 2, 4 and 9, there is a Young diagram λ with n cells such that three things hold. First, for every Young diagram ν with n cells, the Kronecker coefficient of (λ,λ,ν) is positive; here, using the canonical tableaux (arbitrary but fixed bijections from {0,…,n-1} to the cells), this coefficient is the complex dimension of the space of S_n-equivariant linear maps from the Specht representation of ν into the tensor product of the Specht representation of λ with itself, so every irreducible Specht representation of S_n occurs in the tensor square of λ's Specht representation. Second, the Specht representation of λ is irreducible; it is defined as the cyclic subrepresentation, inside the permutation representation on functions from Fin n to Fin(number of rows of λ), generated by the polytabloid, a signed sum over the column-stabilizing subgroup of translates of the indicator of the row-index word. Third, for every finite-dimensional complex irreducible representation ρ of the symmetric group S_n on Fin n, on any module V in the stated universe, there exists an injective S_n-equivariant linear map from ρ into the tensor square of the Specht representation of λ, so this tensor square contains a copy of every irreducible representation.
